Subject: Decode JSON request body when getParsedBody() is an empty array

Visual Editor's save endpoint (since 1.7.2 the PersistenceController
AjaxRoute, split out of the former PersistenceMiddleware) reads the payload
in getJsonPayload() as:

    $payload = $request->getParsedBody();
    if (!is_array($payload)) { $payload = json_decode(...); }

On a frontend POST with Content-Type: application/json, PHP populates
$_POST as an empty array, and TYPO3's ServerRequestFactory sets the parsed
body to that empty array (not null). [] *is* an array, so the !is_array()
guard never falls through to json_decode(): $payload stays [], DataHandler
runs with an empty datamap, and the endpoint returns {"success": true}
while persisting nothing.

This widens the guard to also decode the raw JSON body whenever the parsed
body is an array containing neither 'data' nor 'cmdArray'.

diff --git a/Classes/Backend/Controller/PersistenceController.php b/Classes/Backend/Controller/PersistenceController.php
index 66b2d2e..4db70e2 100644
--- a/Classes/Backend/Controller/PersistenceController.php
+++ b/Classes/Backend/Controller/PersistenceController.php
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@ final readonly class PersistenceController
     private function getJsonPayload(ServerRequestInterface $request): array
     {
         $payload = $request->getParsedBody();
-        if (!is_array($payload)) {
+        if (!is_array($payload) || (!isset($payload['data']) && !isset($payload['cmdArray']))) {
             $payload = json_decode((string)$request->getBody(), true, 512, JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR);
         }
 
